@prefix sagebrain: <https://w3id.org/synapse/sagebrain#> .
@prefix prov:      <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix owl:       <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:      <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@base <https://w3id.org/synapse/sagebrain/governance/provenance_bridge> .

# Bridges sagebrain:derived_from into governanceDUO's provenance layer
# (ontology/imports/governance_layer.ttl, gated behind `make WITH_GOVERNANCE=1`
# same as this module): governanceDUO's derivation-policy builder walks
# prov:wasDerivedFrom* ancestry to compute access control labels, and without
# this sub-property assertion it stops at the Synapse file a sagebrain
# Association/Sample points at, never reaching the Association itself. See
# sagebrain:derived_from's own comment in ontology/main/sagebrain.ttl and
# plans/governance_layer_import.md.
#
# This repo owns this one axiom -- everything else about the provenance layer
# (prov:Activity/prov:Usage and their properties, shape:UsageShape/
# shape:ActivityShape) is imported from governanceDUO, decision D9 of
# plans/governance_layer_import.md: one owner per governance-layer term and
# shape. It lives here, in ontology/governance/, not ontology/main/: the
# default build's DL-checked set does not import prov.ttl, so a bare
# subPropertyOf assertion there would add an undeclared property.
#
# prov:wasDerivedFrom must be declared here too, not left to resolve from
# context: sagebrain's DL-checked set does not import prov.ttl (see above),
# so without this declaration OWLAPI reads the sagebrain:derived_from axiom
# below as an annotation sub-property rather than an object one, and the
# combined OWL 2 DL check fails -- confirmed during governanceDUO's own
# contract-check simulation (plans/governance_layer_import.md).
prov:wasDerivedFrom a owl:ObjectProperty .

sagebrain:derived_from rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:wasDerivedFrom .
